This repository contains no Olympus / OM Digital Solutions firmware. The builder downloads the
official firmware from OM's own server on the user's machine.

Third-party:
- external/oly_fw_analysis (git submodule, fishcu): PEN-F firmware research and MN103 emulator harness,
  used by the developer verification tools only. It is not part of Caduceus and keeps its own licence
  (GPL-3.0 for its code); it is not needed to build or install Caduceus.
- webapp/src/om3.ts, webapp/src/om3names.ts and webapp/tests/om3.test.ts are from Caduceus for OM-3
  (androidfanman/caduceus-om3, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 androidfanman), with a source line added.
- The colour-grain method (CPU grain on the developed photo through the bus window) follows Caduceus for OM-3
  (androidfanman/caduceus-om3, Apache-2.0), research/grain/model.py and firmware/src/xblock.s. The E-P7 code in
  patches/grain_cpu is our own.
- webapp/public/fonts/om3label.woff2: a renamed ASCII subset of DejaVu Sans Condensed (Bitstream Vera
  licence; DejaVu changes public domain), see webapp/public/fonts/FONT-LICENSE.txt.
- 65:24 aspect fixes adapted from flickering-star's work (fork of oly_fw_analysis), with thanks.
  patches/aspect_fix (issue #23) uses that fork's site list and approach (branch ep7-aperture-ar, GPL-3.0);
  the stubs and data there are written for our ids 6/7, see docs/ASPECT.md section 1i.
- Community film recipes are credited to their authors in docs/LIBRARY_V1.md.

